# name: Langton's loops
# description: Langton's self-reproducing loop (1984). Eight states on a von Neumann neighbourhood: a sheathed data path carries instructions round a loop and extrudes an arm that grows, turns and closes into a daughter. A colony fills the space outwards, the interior loops dying as they are walled in.
# palette: 1 = #3C64FF  2 = #E03C3C  3 = #46C846  4 = #E6E024  5 = #E040E0  6 = #F0F0F0  7 = #3CE0E0
states 8; neighbourhood von_neumann 1;
# Langton's 219 transitions, written CNESW -> C' in his own numbering and
# transcribed here as signature literals. Aether's canonical neighbour order
# is north, west, east, south (SPEC #3), so each line reorders his N,E,S,W to
# match; `rot` supplies the three other quarter turns, which is what his
# rotate-4 symmetry means. Anything unlisted keeps its state, as his table
# assumes and SPEC #7 specifies.
0: [0, 0, 0, 0] rot -> 0;
0: [0, 1, 0, 0] rot -> 2;
0: [0, 2, 0, 0] rot -> 0;
